ata/output/ + __pycache__\\n\\n## 4. src/__init__.py (empty)\\n\\n## 5. src/config.py\\nConfiguration module that:\\n- Loads API keys from environment variables (with python-dotenv)\\n- Has a Config dataclass with:\\n  - unstructured_api_key: str\\n  - gemini_api_key: str  \\n  - unstructured_base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io'\\n  - gemini_model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash'\\n  - match_threshold: float = 0.75 (minimum similarity for candidate matching)\\n- Function load_config() that reads from .env and returns Config\\n- Raises clear error if required keys are missing\\n\\n## 6. src/extract/__init__.py (empty)\\n\\n## 7. src/extract/excel_reader.py\\nModule to read Excel files (both shortages and warehouse lists):\\n- Function read_excel(filepath: Path) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - Opens the Excel file with openpyxl\\n  - Auto-detects which sheet has data (skip empty sheets)\\n  - Auto-detects header row (first row with multiple non-empty cells)\\n  - Returns list of dicts with column headers as keys\\n  - Preserves all original values as-is (strings, numbers)\\n  - Handles both Arabic and English column names\\n- Function extract_item_names(rows: list[dict], name_column: str = None) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - If name_column is provided, use it\\n  - Otherwise, auto-detect the column most likely to contain drug names (look for columns with Arabic text, keywords like 'صنف', 'اسم', 'دواء')\\n  - Returns list of {\\\"item_name_raw\\\": str, \\\"source_row\\\": int, \\\"source_file\\\": str}\\n  - Keeps ALL original text including abbreviations, numbers, etc.\\n\\n## 8. src/extract/pdf_reader.py\\nModule to extract drug names from PDF files using Unstructured API:\\n- Function extract_from_pdf(filepath: Path, api_key: str, base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io') -> dict that:\\n  - Uploads PDF to Unstructured API with profile='best', output='elements'\\n  - Handles polling for async jobs (status checking loop)\\n  - Returns the full JSON response